 Also called: Arrow Glyphs, Arrow Plot, Glyph Arrows, Vector Glyphs as Arrows, Vector field arrow visualization
 ## Overview
-Arrow glyphs resolve the direction ambiguity inherent in line-based vector field visualizations by using arrow-shaped primitives that explicitly encode flow direction [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike [Line Glyphs for Vector Field Visualization](2569-line-glyphs-for-vector-field-visualization.md), which suffer from orientation ambiguity, arrow glyphs use triangular faces to allow for 3D shading and clear directional cues [S2, unofficial]. This method is implemented entirely on the GPU to avoid CPU-GPU data transfer, resulting in performance approximately 2x faster than line glyphs (about 10 ms for typical scenes) due to the larger visual size of arrows allowing for lower sampling density [S2, unofficial].
